---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout theme="lab" title="Privacy Policy | Grailmaster" description="Privacy policy and data protection information for grailmaster.com.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x max-w-2xl">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-semibold md:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-[color:var(--text-dim)]">Last updated: August 2026.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
        <div>
          <strong class="text-[color:var(--text)]">1. Controller</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">
            Dr. Axel Schumacher<br />
            Solalindenstr. 84, 81827 München, Germany<br />
            Email:
            <a
              data-site-mail
              data-site-mail-text
              href="#"
              class="link-underline"
              rel="nofollow">parallelspace.advisors [at] gmail.com</a
            >
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">Full details: see the <a href="/imprint" class="link-underline">Imprint</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong class="text-[color:var(--text)]">2. Hosting</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">
            This site is hosted on Cloudflare, Inc. (with servers operated worldwide via
            Cloudflare's network). When you visit this site, Cloudflare automatically processes
            technical data such as your IP address, browser type, and request timestamps to
            deliver the page and protect it against abuse (a "legitimate interest" under Art. 6(1)(f)
            GDPR). This site does not use Cloudflare's optional analytics or advertising products.
            Cloudflare's own privacy policy:
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="link-underline"
              >cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong class="text-[color:var(--text)]">3. Cookies &amp; analytics</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">
            This site does not set tracking or advertising cookies, and does not run any
            third-party analytics or ad-tracking script. Any cookies set are strictly technical
            (e.g. by an embedded form or booking widget listed below, to keep your session
            working) and are not used to build an advertising profile of you. If that ever
            changes, this page will be updated first.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong class="text-[color:var(--text)]">4. Forms, booking, and email signup</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">
            Where this site lets you submit a form, book a call, or join a mailing list, that
            feature is provided by one of the following processors. Each only receives what you
            actively type into that specific form or embed:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-[color:var(--text)]">Tally</strong> (Tally Labs, operating in the
              EU/EEA) — for inquiry and contact forms. Submitting a form is processed under Art.
              6(1)(b) GDPR (steps to respond to your request) or Art. 6(1)(a) (consent), depending
              on the form. Tally's privacy policy:
              <a href="https://tally.so/help/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="link-underline"
                >tally.so/help/privacy-policy</a
              >.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-[color:var(--text)]">Cal.com</strong> (Cal.com, Inc.) — for
              scheduling coaching and consultation calls. Booking a call is processed under Art.
              6(1)(b) GDPR (steps to fulfil your request). Cal.com's privacy policy:
              <a href="https://cal.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="link-underline"
                >cal.com/privacy</a
              >.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-[color:var(--text)]">Brevo</strong> (Sendinblue SAS, France) —
              for waitlists, launch notifications, and the newsletter. Signing up adds your email
              to a mailing list under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR (your consent); every email includes an
              unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing deletes you from that list. Brevo's privacy
              policy:
              <a href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="link-underline"
                >brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy</a
              >.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong class="text-[color:var(--text)]">5. Your rights</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">
            Under GDPR you have the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict processing of
            your personal data, to object to processing, and to data portability. Where
            processing is based on consent (e.g. a newsletter signup), you can withdraw that
            consent at any time, without affecting processing that already happened. To exercise
            any of these rights, contact the email address above. You also have the right to
            lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority — for this site, the competent
            authority is the
            <a href="https://www.lda.bayern.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="link-underline"
              >Bayerisches Landesamt für Datenschutzaufsicht (BayLDA)</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong class="text-[color:var(--text)]">6. Data retention</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">
            Data submitted through a form or booking is kept only as long as needed to handle
            your request, plus any period required by German commercial or tax law where
            applicable. Mailing list entries are kept until you unsubscribe or request deletion.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
